From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: a full-screen task's window is never minimized, and takes the screen's size at once

Broforce launched from PowOS (2026-10-30): its window 0x5400003 (steam_app_274190) was WM_STATE Iconic,
_NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN+FULLSCREEN, unmapped, at 1360x1708 on the unfolded 2268x2440 screen. Opening it showed the
Plasma desktop while its music played.

1. A full-screen Wine/Unity/SDL game minimizes itself when it loses KWin's activation (0031 notes it too).
   handOverMinimize (0036) skipped full-screen tasks, so the minimize stayed: the task showed nothing, and a task
   that never went live handed the minimized window to the desktop (0034). Now a full-screen task's window (opened
   full screen, or a floating one gone full screen) is restored at once, live or not, and the app isn't told
   (the user didn't minimize it). A game that keeps minimizing itself is left so after 3 tries within 2 s: focus()
   (0028) restores it when its task comes to the front.
2. A floating task whose window goes full screen kept the floating task's size until the app made the task full
   screen and its buffers followed. The game was configured to that size (1360x1708 = the 60x70% floating size)
   and kept it. Now fitFullScreen takes the screen's (the output's, folded or unfolded) size at once, until the
   task reports a size of its own that differs from the floating one.
3. A task that never went live and ends (0034) leaves a minimized full-screen window restored and active on the
   desktop, not minimized where nothing shows it.
---
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
index 13608b8..f9b2beb 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -191,10 +191,41 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::handOverMaximize()
 
 void AnlandWindowTask::handOverMinimize()
 {
+    if (!m_window || m_givingBack || !m_window->isMinimized()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (m_fullScreen || m_appFullScreen || m_window->isFullScreen()) {
+        // A full-screen window in its task (a game) is never minimized: the task is what's on screen or not. A
+        // full-screen Wine/Unity/SDL game minimizes ITSELF (WM_CHANGE_STATE iconic) when it loses KWin's activation -
+        // Broforce did on launch (2026-10-30: WM_STATE Iconic, _NET_WM_STATE_HIDDEN+FULLSCREEN, unmapped): its task
+        // then showed nothing, opening it showed the Plasma desktop while its music played, and a task that never
+        // went live because of it handed the minimized window to the desktop (0034). Undone at once, before or after
+        // the task went live, and not told to the app: the user didn't ask for it. Its focus comes with the task's
+        // ("focus", 0028).
+        // HACK: a game that keeps asking (minimizes again every time it's restored while inactive) is left minimized
+        // after a few tries in a row - focus() restores it when its task comes to the front. The real fix is the
+        // game not seeing a focus loss while its task is on screen (Proton's fullscreen focus handling).
+        const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        if (now - m_minimizeUndoneAt > std::chrono::seconds(2)) {
+            m_minimizeUndos = 0;
+        }
+        m_minimizeUndoneAt = now;
+        if (++m_minimizeUndos > 3) {
+            qCWarning(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << "full-screen window keeps minimizing itself: left so until its task takes the focus";
+            return;
+        }
+        qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << "full-screen window minimized itself (live" << m_exported << "): restored, a full-screen task's window is never minimized";
+        QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [w = m_window]() {
+            if (w && !w->isDeleted() && w->isMinimized()) {
+                w->setMinimized(false);
+            }
+        }, Qt::QueuedConnection);
+        return;
+    }
     // A floating task's window minimized by its own request (a client-side bar's minimize button): the task goes into
     // the dock ("minimize <id>"). The window itself is shown again at once - the task shows it, and an unmapped window
     // is a black task when it comes back (0028 restores it on focus as well).
-    if (!m_window || !m_exported || m_givingBack || m_fullScreen || m_appFullScreen || !m_window->isMinimized()) {
+    if (!m_exported) {
         return;
     }
     qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << "asked to be minimized: the task minimizes";
@@ -282,6 +313,14 @@ AnlandWindowTask::~AnlandWindowTask()
             m_window->checkWorkspacePosition(); // still full screen: the screen's size again (kept while exported)
         }
         workspace()->activateWindow(m_window);
+    } else if (m_window && !m_exported && !m_window->isDeleted() && workspace() && m_window->isFullScreen()
+               && m_window->isMinimized()) {
+        // A full-screen window (a game) whose task never went live (0034: the desktop came on screen first) minimized
+        // itself meanwhile - it never had KWin's activation. It stays on the desktop shown and in front, not minimized
+        // where nothing shows it (Broforce: opening it showed the Plasma desktop while its music played, 2026-10-30).
+        qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << "never went live: its minimized full-screen window is restored on the desktop";
+        m_window->setMinimized(false);
+        workspace()->activateWindow(m_window);
     }
 }
 
@@ -677,6 +716,9 @@ bool AnlandWindowTask::setAppFullScreen(bool on)
         return false;
     }
     m_appFullScreen = on;
+    // The floating task's size now: until the app reports the full-screen task's own (fullScreenTaskSize), the
+    // window takes the screen's at once instead of this one.
+    m_floatingTaskSize = on ? taskSize() : QSize();
     // Kept through output changes while the task shows it full screen (as a game's own full-screen task, goLive).
     m_window->setProperty("powosKeepFullScreenGeometry", on);
     qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << (on ? "full screen (the app's own)" : "floating again") << m_window->clientGeometry();
@@ -718,7 +760,7 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::fitFullScreen()
         return;
     }
     const qreal targetScale = m_window->targetScale();
-    const QSize task = taskSize();
+    const QSize task = fullScreenTaskSize();
     if (task.isEmpty() || targetScale <= 0) {
         return;
     }
@@ -734,6 +776,23 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::fitFullScreen()
     scheduleRender(); // drawn at the task's scale until the client commits its new size
 }
 
+QSize AnlandWindowTask::fullScreenTaskSize() const
+{
+    // A floating task whose window went full screen (a game: Unity/Proton maps it windowed, then full screen) is still
+    // the floating task's size until the app has made the task full screen and its buffers follow ("size"). The game
+    // was configured to that size and kept it: Broforce rendered 1360x1708 (the 60x70% floating size) on the unfolded
+    // 2268x2440 screen (2026-10-30). The full-screen task covers the screen, so the window takes the screen's size
+    // (the container: folded or unfolded, as the output is now) at once; the task's own size wins once it differs
+    // from the floating one. Drawn scaled into the old buffers for that moment (scale()/viewport(): fitsWindow).
+    const QSize task = taskSize();
+    if (!m_appFullScreen || m_floatingTaskSize.isEmpty() || task != m_floatingTaskSize || !m_window) {
+        return task;
+    }
+    const LogicalOutput *output = m_window->output();
+    const QSize screen = output ? output->pixelSize() : QSize();
+    return screen.isEmpty() ? task : screen;
+}
+
 void AnlandWindowTask::noteResized()
 {
     // The client committed the size resizeTo asked for: how long it took (the log line after the resize).
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
index 3357631..f978e1b 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
@@ -152,6 +152,7 @@ private:
     void handOverMoveResize();
     void handOverMaximize();
     void handOverMinimize();
+    QSize fullScreenTaskSize() const;
 
     AnlandWindowTasks *m_tasks;
     QPointer<Window> m_window;
@@ -176,6 +177,9 @@ private:
     bool m_stale[MAX_BUFS] = {};
     QSize m_bufferSize;
     QSize m_taskSize; // resizeTo's, empty until the app says one
+    QSize m_floatingTaskSize; // the task's size when its window went full screen (setAppFullScreen), until it changes
+    std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point m_minimizeUndoneAt; // handOverMinimize: a full-screen window's own minimize undone
+    int m_minimizeUndos = 0; // ... how many times in a row (2 s apart at most)
     // Configure -> commit latency of resizeTo's steps (one log line per resize, 500 ms after its last step).
     std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point m_resizeAsked;
     QSizeF m_resizeWanted;
